 >Firstly what do the `real' typesetters/publishers call these?

The publishers I have dealt with here in England uniformly call
these different levels of headinging by capital letters: "A-heading, B-heading",
etc.

Thus,

chapter    A-heading
section    B-heading
subsect    C-heading

and so on.

